# 28 — Contributor ownership: respect prior grants and design Astrid's model

**Start:** [Astrid development skill](../../skills/astrid-dev/SKILL.md). Status, owner and priority belong only in the [catalog](../index.md).

**Vision gaps:** [CA-002 — Contributor ownership](../../vision/gaps/CA-002-contributor-ownership.md) (primary).

## Goal

Make the ambition of **100% contributor ownership in the company behind the collective** credible, fair and legally workable. Crucially, **honour and reconcile Banodoco's earlier published allocations and communicated commitments** before proposing the ownership model for Astrid/the successor collective. This draft grants no new equity.

## Reuse the previous version

Banodoco published an [ownership proposal](https://github.com/banodoco/Banodoco-website/blob/e46641b15f99d9bc26788039c96944e06ffc32b6/ownership/index.html) describing a 1%-per-month, 8.5-year contributor model; [historical grant listings](https://github.com/banodoco/Banodoco-website/blob/e46641b15f99d9bc26788039c96944e06ffc32b6/ownership/data.js) and [contribution-review tools](https://github.com/banodoco/equity-review/blob/5319eadcabe319e6de646b09ed2b6b3bda4e829a/README.md) also exist. These are the starting point, **not** evidence that legal equity was issued or that every individual promise is captured. [Source assessment and unknowns](inputs.md).

## Sequence

1. **Reconcile prior commitments.** Inventory published grants/transfers, direct promises, corrections, recipients and missing periods. Distinguish public proposals, individual commitments, actual approvals and executed legal instruments. Verify sensitive cases privately, preserve source identities and make disputes reviewable. No silent resetting of allocations.
2. **Define succession and rights.** Establish what entity and economics the original grants referred to, and how they map—without unilaterally changing rights—to Astrid or a newly incorporated company. Decide how the lapse, earlier work, ongoing contributions, financing, vesting and dilution should be handled, with appropriate recipient involvement.
3. **Choose a future model.** Compare the original monthly allocation approach with a contributor-held vehicle, direct equity/options or a legally suitable equivalent. Cover contributions in art, software, models, shared knowledge and community work; eligibility, allocation, transparent review, governance, disputes, leavers and investor compatibility. The original percentages/horizon are historical inputs, not automatically renewed terms.
4. **Legally qualify and implement.** Obtain an explicit owner decision, qualified legal/tax advice for actual jurisdictions, recipient consent where required, and an authorized implementation. Publish understandable terms and a privacy-aware record with a repeatable allocation/review process.

## Boundaries and proof

No company structure, cap table, grant amount, legal interpretation or recipient entitlement is decided in this plan. Don't place private identity/financial/legal records in the public repo or issue promises in the name of an unformed company. Completion requires a reconciled, source-backed historic ledger, a documented treatment of prior claims, an approved and legally qualified successor model, and real evidence of authorized implementation and meaningful contested-case handling. Reassess [CA-002](../../vision/gaps/CA-002-contributor-ownership.md) on evidence; finishing the draft alone cannot close it.

